{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The Stan program does not condition on or score any top-level data variable in the `model` block.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program has no parameters, no sampling statements, and no arbitrary `target` manipulation; all top-level data variables are context inputs used to construct generated quantities.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real x;

  real<lower=0> rho;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N, N] cov =   gp_exp_quad_cov(x, alpha, rho)
                     + diag_matrix(rep_vector(1e-10, N));
  matrix[N, N] L_cov = cholesky_decompose(cov);
}

parameters {}
model {}

generated quantities {
  vector[N] f = multi_normal_cholesky_rng(rep_vector(0, N), L_cov);
  array[N] real y = normal_rng(f, sigma);
}
